// An owner that nothing takes is refused where it is written.
//
// A discarded `move(...)` was already refused, but the other two ways to
// produce an owner were not: `new Box();` and a call returning `Box*` compiled,
// ran, and leaked. The managed leak checker then aborted the program at exit
// with a handle number and no hint of where the allocation came from, and the
// raw case leaked in silence.
//
// Arrays are deliberately not covered: the backend releases an array temporary
// at the end of its statement, which tests/array-copy.abs relies on.
//
// Compiled for the diagnostics, so the file never runs. What is still open is
// an owner produced *inside* a larger expression -- `if (make() != null)` --
// which this rule does not see; docs/known-defects.md carries the reproducer.

class Box {
    public int32 value;
}

Box* makeManaged() {
    return new Box();
}

int32 main() {
    new Box();
    makeManaged();
    new raw Box();

    Box* kept = makeManaged();
    return kept.value;
}
